#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:5
#: ef0db3038496403d86ef38ddb476f79c
msgid "OSD based parameter menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:7
#: fa8c83bf69be4254aeb54b690c9d11f5
msgid "This allows to set and adjust parameters using the ArduPilot onboard OSD and an RC transmitter's stick input. There's two additional OSD screens available (OSD5 and OSD6), with 9 \"slots\" each to hold parameters. The screens display a default set of parameters to start with. Additionally, it is possible to change the parameter used in a respective slot directly (on-screen) using stick inputs, or using MAVProxy's osd-module command-line setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:12
#: 54bc029653484b848799e426266cbc8d
msgid "OpenTX/EdgeTX CRSF lua scripts allow access to this feature in some radio transmitters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:15
#: c168a3fc48f04e8f92b95b5d8e786607
msgid "Copter default screens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:24
#: b65d408c489e41c6803a5395ab801af7
msgid "Plane default screens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:31
#: 240145c828c4402cb806d1f8b33c715f
msgid "The RC transmitter's roll and pitch stick input is used to navigate through the screen, pick a parameter and adjust the parameter value. Parameter values can be adjusted in disarmed state only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:34
#: 820f0dd15e0649ad876bbc516d203562
msgid "Additionally there's a \"save and reboot\" button on each screen that allows to save the adjusted settings and reboot the flightcontroller if required. It defaults to \"reboot\", will auto-switch to \"save\" if a parameter value has been altered, and switch back to \"reboot\" after saving is completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:40
#: 70db61f71fb943f9b6514f2ae428794d
msgid "Using the \"save\" button after adjusting a parameter will make the adjustments persistent, otherwise the value will be reset to its prior state after a reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:43
#: f2768ea2f5e64907863d6eac48b91493
msgid "Accessing parameter screens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:45
#: fe60776979194359a460b265e444aed5
msgid "To enable the parameter screens, set :ref:`OSD5_ENABLE <OSD5_ENABLE>` and :ref:`OSD6_ENABLE <OSD6_ENABLE>` = 1. Parameter screens can be accessed in the same way the conventional osd screens are accessed. See the documentation on :ref:`OSD screens and switching <screen-switching>` for reference. When one of the parameter screens is selected, adjustments can be made in disarmed state only. If a parameter screen is selected inflight, the screen allows display only. This allows live monitoring of automatic parameter adjustments, i.e. when performing autotune procedures or automatic servo trims."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:52
#: 778681cc599145b295a7a675520558b2
msgid "For systems not using an actual OSD, as when using CRSF with no OSD or DJI OSD, and running OpenTX transmitters with CRSF configuration script, setting :ref:`OSD_TYPE<OSD_TYPE>` =3 (MSP), will allow the OpenTX CRSF script on the transmitter to change these parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:55
#: 2215aa6c6ecf4da88e5b8e1e74c32b28
msgid "Menu navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:57
#: 5d1af3b280e24fb3b6624f68896c7dd0
msgid "Use the RC transmitter's roll and pitch input to navigate through the parameter screen. UP / DOWN and LEFT / RIGHT will navigate through the screen's parameter slots. The selected parameter will blink. Move right on the selected parameter to adjust its value using up or down stick input. Leave the selection with left roll stick input. On a typical mode 2 type transmitter this would be the right gimbal stick:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:68
#: a07acea7b5ab41a9bf572fcb169223b9
msgid "Parameter slot scroll-selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:70
#: 3c9dcac2e2254fec951873ba5ec0bf6f
msgid "Holding roll right for > 3 seconds on a parameter's value will highlight both the selected parameter and its value (blink). This allows you to scroll through the full list of parameters and place another parameter into that respective slot using pitch up and down stick input. Move left to exit parameter selection and get back into standard screen navigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:76
#: 2e7d89d30eb44deab999fee0ac39f540
msgid "OSD based parameter adjustment is designed to allow basic adjustments without any additional data link or GCS setup required. However, some parameters with exceptionally wide value ranges, as well as complex bitmap-type parameters might not be ideal for adjustment using parameter OSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:81
#: 34261bd7dea644038b15a562b7c57a03
msgid "Parameter range, increment and type-mnemonics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-paramosd.rst:83
#: f2d21bf97561463c9d620d280d68c3f4
msgid "OSD based parameter menu uses parameter metadata to estimate a useful value range and incrementation for each parameter. Additionally, support for the display of human-readable abbreviations instead of numeric values is provided for the following parameter types:"
msgstr ""

